usage: envctl get [file] <KEY>

Prints the decoded value of KEY followed by a newline and exits 1 when KEY has
no active definition. File values are parsed with quote-aware escape and
comment handling; malformed quoted values exit 2. Multiline values print in
full. Variable references remain literal. --env returns the environment value
as stored.

Flags:
  --env                 use the process environment instead of a file
  --redact              mask secret-looking values
  --raw                 shorthand for --redact=never --show-control-chars
  --show-control-chars  print control bytes as they are
  --paranoid            apply the entropy bar to every value

Full reference: man envctl
